      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can confirm something like this happened to me -- I eventually had to set all the eyelook values to a number that would still look alright if it were swapped to its negative value, because inside VRChat itself that's how far it would actually go.   I don't totally have my head around whether it's the eyes that are swapped, or the look directions, or the positive/negative signs on the numbers that the user enters, but any asymmetrical left/right values definitely show up inside VRChat as the opposite of how they appeared in the Unity editor.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
